1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,083
[Mr. Frohicky] ...Well,
they try in their own way,

2
00:00:04,083 --> 00:00:07,250
but not one of them
I would consider a fine chef.

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:10,250
Kai can defrost pizza.

4
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:11,500
Poorly.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,291
Had lots of time to learn
how to cook

6
00:00:13,291 --> 00:00:14,791
in the Land of Lost Things.

7
00:00:14,791 --> 00:00:17,333
Ton of ingredients
show up there.

8
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:19,583
I once found a tray
of diced garlic.

9
00:00:19,583 --> 00:00:21,541
Oh, I reeked for a month,

10
00:00:21,541 --> 00:00:24,000
but, mm... delicious!

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,208
Well, having you here

12
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:27,041
has made the part of my job

13
00:00:27,041 --> 00:00:29,583
where I'm expected to be
a Master Chef easier.

14
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:30,791
[chuckling]

15
00:00:30,791 --> 00:00:35,333
Now, if you could learn
to polish a floor...

16
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,333
Come on, play with us!

17
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,708
Oh, I'm not that healed yet.

18
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:41,208
I'll just watch you two.

19
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:43,916
[kids laughing playfully]

20
00:00:45,041 --> 00:00:46,625
Ah, refreshments.

21
00:00:49,375 --> 00:00:50,375
Mm.

22
00:00:50,375 --> 00:00:52,250
Ah, I've been parched.

23
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,791
Glad to you see you
doing so well, Rontu.

24
00:00:55,791 --> 00:00:56,833
We, uh...

25
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,666
had some doubts
you would pull through.

26
00:00:58,666 --> 00:01:00,791
You are not the only one.

27
00:01:00,791 --> 00:01:03,875
I must confess,
I had lost hope myself.

28
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:06,041
Well, fetid salamander broth

29
00:01:06,041 --> 00:01:09,333
is such a strong,
natural medicine,

30
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:12,208
it could grow skin
on a Greenbone Warrior!

31
00:01:12,208 --> 00:01:14,583
[chuckling politely] Yes...

32
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:16,500
though the broth did taste...

33
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,208
[clearing throat] ...fine,

34
00:01:18,208 --> 00:01:21,083
my return was more spiritual.

35
00:01:21,083 --> 00:01:23,416
I spoke to an old love,

36
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,541
and discovered a new purpose.

37
00:01:25,541 --> 00:01:28,083
My work on this plane
is not done.

38
00:01:28,083 --> 00:01:30,125
Nope, pretty sure
it was the broth.

39
00:01:31,125 --> 00:01:33,541
[sniffing] That smells good.

40
00:01:33,541 --> 00:01:35,083
Geo, are you cooking here now?

41
00:01:35,083 --> 00:01:36,208
Yup,

42
00:01:36,208 --> 00:01:38,083
but I have to go out
and buy ingredients,

43
00:01:38,083 --> 00:01:40,708
not wait for a geyser
to burp them up.

44
00:01:40,708 --> 00:01:42,625
Well, apparently,
that's more reliable

45
00:01:42,625 --> 00:01:46,000
than sending Arin's parents off
with a grocery list.

46
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,583
They've been gone for--

47
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:49,041
[panting]

48
00:01:49,041 --> 00:01:51,125
There was an attack
in the Crossroads!

49
00:01:51,125 --> 00:01:53,083
Some kind of energy monster!

50
00:01:53,083 --> 00:01:54,583
Energy Monster?

51
00:01:54,583 --> 00:01:55,916
Came out of nowhere.

52
00:01:55,916 --> 00:01:57,333
We got people to safety,

53
00:01:57,333 --> 00:01:58,791
but then it just disappeared

54
00:01:58,791 --> 00:02:00,500
as weirdly as it appeared.

55
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,166
Smashed the whole place up.

56
00:02:02,166 --> 00:02:03,541
And this monster kept you

57
00:02:03,541 --> 00:02:06,041
from getting
the fermented beetles why?

58
00:02:06,041 --> 00:02:08,875
No, they did the right thing,
Mr. Frohicky.

59
00:02:08,875 --> 00:02:10,541
But an Energy monster?

60
00:02:10,541 --> 00:02:13,416
Ras stole scrolls
about containing energy.

61
00:02:13,416 --> 00:02:16,708
Maybe the puzzle pieces
are all in a row...

62
00:02:16,708 --> 00:02:18,958
Um, "falling into place."

63
00:02:18,958 --> 00:02:20,166
Ducks are in a row,

64
00:02:20,166 --> 00:02:21,916
pieces fall into place.

65
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:24,541
I... I knew that.

66
00:02:30,666 --> 00:02:32,583
Did you see the Monster
that attacked,

67
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:33,583
and where it went?

68
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:34,458
Saw it?

69
00:02:34,458 --> 00:02:36,625
Dang near blasted my hair off!

70
00:02:36,625 --> 00:02:40,250
Then the thing just evaporated
into thin air.

71
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,416
[scanner warbling]

72
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:53,041
Not suspicious behavior at all.

73
00:02:53,041 --> 00:02:54,125
[♪♪♪]

74
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:02,166
[grunting with effort]

75
00:03:02,166 --> 00:03:03,625
[elemental powers shorting]

76
00:03:05,083 --> 00:03:07,166
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

77
00:03:07,166 --> 00:03:08,375
♪ So much to see ♪

78
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:11,416
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

79
00:03:11,416 --> 00:03:12,875
♪ Together we will rise ♪

80
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:14,375
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

81
00:03:14,375 --> 00:03:15,916
♪ Together we will rise ♪

82
00:03:15,916 --> 00:03:17,833
♪ For what's right ♪♪

83
00:03:20,958 --> 00:03:23,208
[Cole groaning]

84
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:29,000
[crowd shouting with effort]

85
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:35,208
[Cole groaning]

86
00:03:35,208 --> 00:03:36,666
Anyone--

87
00:03:36,666 --> 00:03:37,833
ow--

88
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:39,958
see where that person
in the mask ran off to?

89
00:03:39,958 --> 00:03:41,916
[mumbling uncertainly]

90
00:03:41,916 --> 00:03:42,958
[groaning]

91
00:03:42,958 --> 00:03:45,625
Well, looks like
I stumbled into something

92
00:03:45,625 --> 00:03:47,541
painfully nefarious...

93
00:03:47,541 --> 00:03:49,041
[audible smooching]

94
00:03:49,041 --> 00:03:50,625
Uh...

95
00:03:50,625 --> 00:03:52,333
you two done yet?

96
00:03:52,333 --> 00:03:54,000
You remember everything now?

97
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,333
Not everything.

98
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:57,125
As soon as that machine
processed,

99
00:03:57,125 --> 00:03:58,541
I got a flood of memories,

100
00:03:58,541 --> 00:04:00,541
but more keep popping up,

101
00:04:00,541 --> 00:04:02,291
and I don't know
what I don't know,

102
00:04:02,291 --> 00:04:05,000
so who knows how many
more memories I'm gonna recall.

103
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:05,958
But you're back?

104
00:04:05,958 --> 00:04:07,750
I'm back.

105
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,166
So, uh, does that mean

106
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:11,125
you remember the time
you fought Bolobo

107
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,625
in just your underpants?

108
00:04:12,625 --> 00:04:13,458
That one...

109
00:04:13,458 --> 00:04:15,125
that one's not ringing a bell.

110
00:04:15,125 --> 00:04:17,791
What about when you convinced
a bunch of video game fan boys

111
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:19,000
to dress up like you,

112
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,458
and talk about
how awesome you were?

113
00:04:20,458 --> 00:04:21,333
Nope.

114
00:04:21,333 --> 00:04:22,458
Not that one either.

115
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:23,750
Are you sure?

116
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:26,041
Maybe you just don't want
to remember those stories?

117
00:04:26,041 --> 00:04:27,250
'Cause if I were you,

118
00:04:27,250 --> 00:04:28,375
I'd try to forget them, too.

119
00:04:28,375 --> 00:04:29,833
No, I'm serious.

120
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:32,541
It feels like my memories
are "healing",

121
00:04:32,541 --> 00:04:34,833
just repopulating my mind.

122
00:04:34,833 --> 00:04:37,458
And who erased your memories
in the first place?

123
00:04:37,458 --> 00:04:40,666
That... I still don't remember,

124
00:04:40,666 --> 00:04:42,375
yet,

125
00:04:42,375 --> 00:04:43,333
but I'm sure it'll--

126
00:04:43,333 --> 00:04:46,041
[gasping] Oh my!

127
00:04:46,041 --> 00:04:48,625
[sobbing uncontrollably]

128
00:04:48,625 --> 00:04:50,875
Uh... you okay, buddy?

129
00:04:50,875 --> 00:04:53,291
Mr. Slowthers!

130
00:04:53,291 --> 00:04:54,750
[sobbing]

131
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:56,708
Poor Mr. Slowthers.

132
00:04:56,708 --> 00:04:59,250
Who is Mr. Slowthers?

133
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:01,125
My turtle! [sniffling]

134
00:05:01,125 --> 00:05:04,958
My pet turtle I had
when I was a little kid!

135
00:05:04,958 --> 00:05:06,333
He ran away,

136
00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:08,916
and I couldn't catch up to him!

137
00:05:08,916 --> 00:05:11,041
You couldn't catch up to a...

138
00:05:11,041 --> 00:05:12,416
turtle?

139
00:05:12,416 --> 00:05:13,583
Apparently,

140
00:05:13,583 --> 00:05:15,416
I wasn't very good at running
as a kid, okay?

141
00:05:15,416 --> 00:05:17,208
Leave me alone! [sobbing]

142
00:05:17,208 --> 00:05:18,375
I know getting
your memories back

143
00:05:18,375 --> 00:05:19,750
in weird bursts like this

144
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:21,500
has got to be a shock,

145
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,250
and I'm sure Mr. Slowthers

146
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,833
found a new safe place
somewhere,

147
00:05:25,833 --> 00:05:27,166
but we gotta do the same.

148
00:05:27,166 --> 00:05:30,166
The Administration is not
going to stop looking for us.

149
00:05:30,166 --> 00:05:31,500
Come on.

150
00:05:34,541 --> 00:05:35,708
[Jay whispering]
I bet these robots

151
00:05:35,708 --> 00:05:37,291
are guarding all the exits.

152
00:05:37,291 --> 00:05:40,083
Curses on whoever
came up with these things.

153
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:41,250
<i>[Lead Agent, on walkie]</i>
<i>Attention, Delta League,</i>

154
00:05:41,250 --> 00:05:43,083
<i>another</i>
<i>unauthorized energy being</i>

155
00:05:43,083 --> 00:05:45,125
<i>spotted in Region 412.</i>

156
00:05:45,125 --> 00:05:46,666
<i>Assemble a convoy!</i>

157
00:05:46,666 --> 00:05:47,833
Copy that.

158
00:05:49,041 --> 00:05:49,958
[weapons charging]

159
00:05:54,333 --> 00:05:56,458
[revving engines]

160
00:05:57,541 --> 00:05:59,541
Agents, roll out!

161
00:05:59,541 --> 00:06:00,833
[tires squealing]

162
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:06,125
[distant wailing]

163
00:06:06,125 --> 00:06:07,625
[Lloyd screaming]

164
00:06:16,166 --> 00:06:18,166
[gasping]

165
00:06:18,166 --> 00:06:19,958
[roots stretching]

166
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,625
[♪♪♪]

167
00:06:51,208 --> 00:06:52,458
[gasping]

168
00:07:01,125 --> 00:07:02,750
[gasping]

169
00:07:05,250 --> 00:07:06,291
Wha...

170
00:07:06,291 --> 00:07:07,583
[grunting]

171
00:07:08,583 --> 00:07:10,041
Hello?

172
00:07:10,041 --> 00:07:11,625
Where'd you go?

173
00:07:11,625 --> 00:07:12,791
What was all that?

174
00:07:12,791 --> 00:07:13,916
[wind gusting]

175
00:07:13,916 --> 00:07:16,291
You're not gonna explain
the meaning of that?

176
00:07:16,291 --> 00:07:19,958
It looked like a forest,
sharing energy?

177
00:07:19,958 --> 00:07:21,833
Helping other trees out?

178
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:23,875
Hello?

179
00:07:23,875 --> 00:07:26,875
What was I supposed to learn
from that?

180
00:07:26,875 --> 00:07:29,666
[tween Lloyd]
Oh, you're gonna find out...

181
00:07:29,666 --> 00:07:31,541
Another version of me?

182
00:07:31,541 --> 00:07:34,208
But... I don't recognize you.

183
00:07:34,208 --> 00:07:35,291
Of course you don't.

184
00:07:35,291 --> 00:07:37,125
I never existed.

185
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,333
I am the you
you skipped over,

186
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:41,875
but on this journey,

187
00:07:41,875 --> 00:07:44,833
you have to know
everything about your life...

188
00:07:44,833 --> 00:07:47,875
even paths not walked.

189
00:07:47,875 --> 00:07:48,833
My path.

190
00:07:48,833 --> 00:07:50,666
You're the age I skipped over

191
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:52,500
because of the Tomorrow's Tea.

192
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:53,791
The age when I was
supposed to hear

193
00:07:53,791 --> 00:07:55,500
the calling
of the Whispering Wood.

194
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:58,875
Pleased to finally... meet you.

195
00:08:04,333 --> 00:08:06,458
[Euphrasia] Uh, is this right?

196
00:08:06,458 --> 00:08:08,166
I don't feel the balance you--

197
00:08:08,166 --> 00:08:09,166
Arin?

198
00:08:10,083 --> 00:08:11,750
Sorry, I just...

199
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:12,916
He's been in there all night.

200
00:08:14,041 --> 00:08:16,250
I'm sure he's fine.

201
00:08:17,291 --> 00:08:19,375
Okay, not sure,

202
00:08:19,375 --> 00:08:22,000
but isn't that
why we're training?

203
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,083
To try not to focus
on what's out of our control?

204
00:08:24,083 --> 00:08:25,958
Yeah. Okay.

205
00:08:25,958 --> 00:08:28,083
So your stance is slightly off.

206
00:08:28,083 --> 00:08:30,458
The twist shouldn't
put pressure on your knee,

207
00:08:30,458 --> 00:08:32,000
you'll get injured that way.

208
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,125
It should come from your core,

209
00:08:34,125 --> 00:08:34,958
like this...

210
00:08:40,416 --> 00:08:41,583
Arin,

211
00:08:41,583 --> 00:08:44,250
I notice you have red streaks
in your tornado.

212
00:08:44,250 --> 00:08:45,333
Why is that?

213
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:47,208
Uh...

214
00:08:47,208 --> 00:08:48,750
No one else has them?

215
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,291
Is that weird?

216
00:08:50,291 --> 00:08:52,125
I've never
encountered it before.

217
00:08:52,125 --> 00:08:54,750
Is my Spinjitzu corrupted
or something?

218
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:56,833
Did training with Ras
do something bad to me?

219
00:08:56,833 --> 00:08:58,958
I'm sure there's no reason
to be alarmed.

220
00:08:58,958 --> 00:09:00,208
I'd just like to study it more--

221
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:01,208
[crowd of Acona chittering]

222
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:02,375
The Acona?

223
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:04,916
[chittering urgently]

224
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,791
I'm getting the sense
they want us to go with them.

225
00:09:08,791 --> 00:09:11,500
Are we going to just
leave Lloyd?

226
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,625
We'll come back,

227
00:09:12,625 --> 00:09:14,458
but if these beings need help,

228
00:09:14,458 --> 00:09:17,250
Lloyd would want us
to help them.

229
00:09:19,416 --> 00:09:22,583
[tires squealing]

230
00:09:23,666 --> 00:09:26,083
We're here looking into reports

231
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:29,000
of a monster
on an unlicensed rampage.

232
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,250
Did you report a monster?

233
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:33,083
Because there's clearly
no ongoing rampage.

234
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:41,541
Filing a false report
is a severe policy violation,

235
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:43,125
punishable by being made
to fill out many reports

236
00:09:43,125 --> 00:09:45,333
about the false report.

237
00:09:45,333 --> 00:09:47,625
Do you have anything to say
in your defense?

238
00:09:47,625 --> 00:09:49,250
[Lead Loyalist]
Here's the situation--

239
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:51,666
I'm taking control
of your convoy.

240
00:09:51,666 --> 00:09:54,708
You've got one chance
to give your vehicles to me.

241
00:09:54,708 --> 00:09:55,916
If not,

242
00:09:55,916 --> 00:09:58,125
I take them by force,

243
00:09:58,125 --> 00:10:00,083
which will go badly for you.

244
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,250
Ha!

245
00:10:02,250 --> 00:10:04,208
Look, not only are you unarmed,

246
00:10:04,208 --> 00:10:06,291
and badly outnumbered,

247
00:10:06,291 --> 00:10:09,416
but you've clearly got no idea
who you're dealing with.

248
00:10:09,416 --> 00:10:12,208
We're from The Administration!

249
00:10:12,208 --> 00:10:14,083
[Lead Loyalist] I warned you.

250
00:10:14,083 --> 00:10:15,458
[snapping fingers]

251
00:10:15,458 --> 00:10:16,416
Huah!
[charging weapons]

252
00:10:17,416 --> 00:10:19,958
[Lead Loyalist]
You're the one with no idea--

253
00:10:19,958 --> 00:10:22,625
no idea how many
of our secret society

254
00:10:22,625 --> 00:10:25,041
have infiltrated
every organization

255
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,583
across the Merged Lands.

256
00:10:26,583 --> 00:10:27,916
Bonnie, no!

257
00:10:27,916 --> 00:10:30,500
You love stamping C-01 permits!

258
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,791
You always smile--

259
00:10:31,791 --> 00:10:34,000
[Loyalist #1] I was faking it,

260
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,083
every single time.

261
00:10:37,583 --> 00:10:39,166
[Lead Loyalist] Attack!

262
00:10:39,166 --> 00:10:41,041
[blasting and shouting]

263
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:46,125
Ah!

264
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,583
Ugh! Ah!

265
00:10:50,583 --> 00:10:52,500
[Nya]
We've gotta get out there!

266
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:54,375
Which side would we even join?

267
00:10:58,416 --> 00:10:59,666
We need to see
how this plays out.

268
00:10:59,666 --> 00:11:00,708
[Kai] He's right.

269
00:11:00,708 --> 00:11:01,791
Let's find out what's going on.

270
00:11:04,416 --> 00:11:06,208
[Lead Agent] Agents, retreat!

271
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:07,416
[yelping in panic]

272
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:12,041
[Lead Loyalist]
We've got what we need.

273
00:11:12,041 --> 00:11:14,041
[whistling]

274
00:11:14,041 --> 00:11:15,750
Mech Drivers,
you know what to do!

275
00:11:17,666 --> 00:11:18,583
[smashing]

276
00:11:27,041 --> 00:11:28,333
[Lead Loyalist] Success!

277
00:11:28,333 --> 00:11:29,791
All hail the Good Empress!

278
00:11:29,791 --> 00:11:31,583
"Good Empress"?

279
00:11:31,583 --> 00:11:33,041
As in Beatrix,

280
00:11:33,041 --> 00:11:35,333
the whacked-out,
power-hungry maniac?

281
00:11:35,333 --> 00:11:36,291
She sounds kinda fun.

282
00:11:36,291 --> 00:11:37,375
-No.
-She's not.

283
00:11:37,375 --> 00:11:38,416
[Lead Loyalist] Come!

284
00:11:38,416 --> 00:11:39,625
We must find the weapon piece!

285
00:11:39,625 --> 00:11:40,916
[Nya] Weapon? Great...

286
00:11:40,916 --> 00:11:43,625
Last time Beatrix got her hands
on a super weapon,

287
00:11:43,625 --> 00:11:46,208
she triggered a world-ending
series of MergeQuakes!

288
00:11:46,208 --> 00:11:47,333
That was her?

289
00:11:47,333 --> 00:11:48,958
That was messed up!

290
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:50,708
Whatever this new "weapon" is,

291
00:11:50,708 --> 00:11:52,875
we have to keep it
out of her hands.

292
00:11:55,625 --> 00:11:58,500
[chittering urgently]

293
00:11:59,833 --> 00:12:01,791
[blasts sizzling]

294
00:12:01,791 --> 00:12:03,791
[chittering in distress]

295
00:12:09,625 --> 00:12:11,208
[snarling]

296
00:12:15,458 --> 00:12:17,166
[growling]

297
00:12:20,291 --> 00:12:23,250
[bellowing]

298
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:24,625
[branches cracking]

299
00:12:25,541 --> 00:12:28,000
[foliage crumbling]

300
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,708
Ninja... Go!

301
00:12:33,375 --> 00:12:34,291
[bellowing]

302
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:40,000
[Zane] Ah!

303
00:12:47,166 --> 00:12:48,208
[snarling]

304
00:12:48,208 --> 00:12:49,791
[gasping]

305
00:12:49,791 --> 00:12:51,166
Aw...

306
00:12:52,541 --> 00:12:54,875
[leaves crumbling]

307
00:12:54,875 --> 00:12:56,041
[bellowing]

308
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:09,916
[♪♪♪]

309
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,750
How can a tree
be growing underground

310
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:19,625
with no sunlight?

311
00:13:19,625 --> 00:13:21,291
-It's--
-[Jay] It's madness.

312
00:13:21,291 --> 00:13:22,916
The Land of Madness!

313
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:37,708
[Lead Loyalist] This is it.

314
00:13:42,791 --> 00:13:44,458
Behold!

315
00:13:44,458 --> 00:13:47,041
A portion of
the Weapon of Desolation!

316
00:13:47,041 --> 00:13:49,416
The Good Empress
is one step closer

317
00:13:49,416 --> 00:13:52,750
to making her triumphant return!

318
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:54,208
[Loyalists cheering]

319
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:55,583
[Lead Loyalist] Pack it up!

320
00:13:55,583 --> 00:13:56,583
We move.

321
00:14:04,166 --> 00:14:06,875
[laughing loudly]

322
00:14:06,875 --> 00:14:08,208
[laughter muffled]

323
00:14:09,833 --> 00:14:10,833
[Jay laughing uncontrollably]

324
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:13,166
[slightly muffled,
still very loud]

325
00:14:13,166 --> 00:14:14,791
[laughter reverberating]

326
00:14:14,791 --> 00:14:15,958
[Kai whispering]
What are you doing?

327
00:14:15,958 --> 00:14:19,291
Hee-hee-he hit every branch
on the way down!

328
00:14:19,291 --> 00:14:20,291
[cackling]

329
00:14:20,291 --> 00:14:21,291
[Nya] What?!

330
00:14:21,291 --> 00:14:22,916
Ninja are here!
[weapon charging]

331
00:14:22,916 --> 00:14:24,541
[laughing]

332
00:14:24,541 --> 00:14:26,500
I'm sorry, I can't help it!

333
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,416
A memory just suddenly hit me!

334
00:14:28,416 --> 00:14:31,458
This time, I hid Cole's cake
at the top of a tree!

335
00:14:31,458 --> 00:14:32,833
He slipped and fell,

336
00:14:32,833 --> 00:14:35,416
and hit every single branch
on the way down!

337
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:36,916
-H'ah!
-H'yah!

338
00:14:36,916 --> 00:14:38,000
[laughing]

339
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,833
[chuckling]
That was pretty funny.

340
00:14:39,833 --> 00:14:41,291
[Nya] H'yah!

341
00:14:41,291 --> 00:14:42,625
[Lead Loyalist] Cover my back!

342
00:14:43,583 --> 00:14:45,041
[Nya] Huah! H'yah!

343
00:14:45,041 --> 00:14:46,791
[Kai] Ooh-ah! H'ah!

344
00:14:46,791 --> 00:14:48,375
H'yah!

345
00:14:48,375 --> 00:14:50,666
I'll take that, thank you!

346
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:51,583
[power surging]

347
00:14:51,583 --> 00:14:53,625
[Kai screaming]

348
00:14:53,625 --> 00:14:54,625
[screams echoing]

349
00:14:54,625 --> 00:14:55,541
Ah!

350
00:14:55,541 --> 00:14:56,541
[Nya] Oof!

351
00:14:58,125 --> 00:14:59,833
-[Jay] Nya!
-[Nya] I'm fine!

352
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:01,333
They're getting away!

353
00:15:01,333 --> 00:15:03,333
[activating device]

354
00:15:03,333 --> 00:15:04,500
-[energy detonating]
-[Ninja] Ah!

355
00:15:07,625 --> 00:15:08,708
[slamming force field]

356
00:15:08,708 --> 00:15:10,541
[frustrated grunting]

357
00:15:10,541 --> 00:15:12,541
What happened to you
back there?

358
00:15:12,541 --> 00:15:13,875
[Kai] I touched that thing,

359
00:15:13,875 --> 00:15:15,583
and my body was flooded

360
00:15:15,583 --> 00:15:18,083
with uncontrollable
Elemental Energy.

361
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,583
Real weird.

362
00:15:19,583 --> 00:15:22,250
Whatever
a "Weapon of Desolation" is,

363
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:24,083
we can't let it get to Beatrix!

364
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,541
[Arc Dragon stomping]

365
00:15:27,541 --> 00:15:29,416
[thudding of battle]

366
00:15:32,625 --> 00:15:33,916
[foliage crumbling]

367
00:15:33,916 --> 00:15:35,458
[monster snarling]

368
00:15:39,333 --> 00:15:40,833
[Acona chittering]

369
00:15:47,083 --> 00:15:47,958
[Arin] Ah!

370
00:15:50,916 --> 00:15:51,916
[gasping]

371
00:15:51,916 --> 00:15:54,416
[chittering]

372
00:15:56,083 --> 00:15:57,125
Huah!

373
00:15:59,708 --> 00:16:02,125
Ugh!
That kinda worked.

374
00:16:06,333 --> 00:16:08,541
[Arin]
If I could do it faster...

375
00:16:08,541 --> 00:16:10,041
Hold it, I got an idea!

376
00:16:10,041 --> 00:16:12,208
When I say when,
toss me rocks!

377
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:14,958
Now!

378
00:16:22,125 --> 00:16:23,791
It's working.
Keep 'em coming!

379
00:16:28,916 --> 00:16:30,750
[bellowing]

380
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:41,625
[Zane] H'ah!

381
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:43,250
[Zane grunting with effort]

382
00:16:44,625 --> 00:16:45,958
Huah!

383
00:16:50,791 --> 00:16:52,458
[Arin] Phew!

384
00:16:52,458 --> 00:16:54,500
[gasping in exhaustion]

385
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:55,583
[groaning]

386
00:17:00,125 --> 00:17:01,375
Arin!

387
00:17:01,375 --> 00:17:03,875
That was beyond
all predictive models.

388
00:17:03,875 --> 00:17:06,583
No one has ever used spinjitzu
that way.

389
00:17:06,583 --> 00:17:08,291
It shouldn't even be possible.

390
00:17:09,791 --> 00:17:11,958
[sighing] I need a nap.

391
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:15,875
The monsters have returned
to an energy state.

392
00:17:15,875 --> 00:17:17,666
They will come back,

393
00:17:17,666 --> 00:17:18,791
and there's no telling

394
00:17:18,791 --> 00:17:20,500
if Arin will be able
to stop them again.

395
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:23,458
[bellowing wearily]

396
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,666
Lloyd is our only hope.

397
00:17:26,666 --> 00:17:28,875
If he doesn't succeed
in his trial,

398
00:17:28,875 --> 00:17:31,083
the Whispering Wood
will be lost.

399
00:17:34,750 --> 00:17:36,041
[♪♪♪]

400
00:17:36,041 --> 00:17:37,250
[Wyldfyre] I'm not saying

401
00:17:37,250 --> 00:17:39,666
you're the coolest dragon
I've ever seen now, Riyu,

402
00:17:39,666 --> 00:17:42,833
but you're not not the coolest
dragon I've ever seen!

403
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:44,250
[replying
in grumbling language]

404
00:17:45,458 --> 00:17:46,750
[grumbling language]

405
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:47,750
[roaring]

406
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:50,458
Whoa-ho!

407
00:17:50,458 --> 00:17:52,083
But all that energy
he absorbed.

408
00:17:52,083 --> 00:17:53,333
Are you sure he's okay?

409
00:17:54,375 --> 00:17:56,750
Let me answer your question
with a question.

410
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:58,541
How many times
do I need to tell you

411
00:17:58,541 --> 00:18:00,583
I'm not a dragon doctor?

412
00:18:00,583 --> 00:18:01,916
All that Elemental Energy

413
00:18:01,916 --> 00:18:04,208
must be what triggered
Riyu's new form.

414
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:05,333
Still doesn't explain

415
00:18:05,333 --> 00:18:06,875
who released the monster
from its cage

416
00:18:06,875 --> 00:18:08,083
or why?

417
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:10,375
It has to be
that masked guy I chased, right?

418
00:18:10,375 --> 00:18:12,125
But who's under the mask?

419
00:18:12,125 --> 00:18:14,916
Someone who knew
the airship's layout.

420
00:18:14,916 --> 00:18:16,250
One of the Explorers?

421
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:17,833
No, that makes no sense.

422
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:19,583
The Explorers were desperate

423
00:18:19,583 --> 00:18:20,708
to haul that monster
back to Ninjago,

424
00:18:20,708 --> 00:18:22,416
and put it on display.

425
00:18:22,416 --> 00:18:24,000
Why would one of them
release it?

426
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,041
[blowing raspberry]
Nothing those weirdos do

427
00:18:26,041 --> 00:18:27,041
makes sense.

428
00:18:29,583 --> 00:18:30,875
Speaking of...

429
00:18:30,875 --> 00:18:32,041
look who's here.

430
00:18:32,041 --> 00:18:34,625
I say, if you still want
a ride back to Ninjago,

431
00:18:34,625 --> 00:18:37,416
we will be leaving forthwith.

432
00:18:37,416 --> 00:18:38,291
Yes.

433
00:18:38,291 --> 00:18:39,583
Ever since someone--

434
00:18:39,583 --> 00:18:40,666
[Riyu grunting innocently]

435
00:18:40,666 --> 00:18:42,000
--destroyed our specimen,

436
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,291
there's no point in staying

437
00:18:43,291 --> 00:18:45,666
in this benighted
hayseed village.

438
00:18:45,666 --> 00:18:47,625
Best return
to the Explorer's Clubhouse

439
00:18:47,625 --> 00:18:51,333
and await another chance
to secure a glorious legacy.

440
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:54,125
Can't get a decent cuppa
round here anyway.

441
00:18:54,125 --> 00:18:55,375
Peasants.

442
00:18:55,375 --> 00:18:58,250
We do still need to get back
to the other Ninja

443
00:18:58,250 --> 00:18:59,750
as quickly as we can.

444
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:01,625
We just need to resupply,

445
00:19:01,625 --> 00:19:03,333
then we'll be on our way.

446
00:19:03,333 --> 00:19:05,208
[Umbrasylvan Grand Inquisitor]
No, you will not!

447
00:19:09,416 --> 00:19:10,750
Who are you supposed to be?

448
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:13,291
Some kind of headwear salesman?

449
00:19:13,291 --> 00:19:14,958
[blowing trumpet fanfare]

450
00:19:14,958 --> 00:19:16,458
Presenting...

451
00:19:16,458 --> 00:19:20,875
the Grand Inquisitor
Of Umbrasylvis!

452
00:19:22,291 --> 00:19:23,666
Outsiders!

453
00:19:23,666 --> 00:19:26,666
Nothing good ever comes
from outsiders!

454
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,416
Well, that's just nonsense.

455
00:19:28,416 --> 00:19:30,125
If we Explorers
had never come,

456
00:19:30,125 --> 00:19:32,875
you'd never have been discovered
by anyone.

457
00:19:32,875 --> 00:19:34,375
Where would you be then?

458
00:19:34,375 --> 00:19:36,791
Someone released a monster
on purpose

459
00:19:36,791 --> 00:19:39,458
to wreak havoc in our fair town!

460
00:19:39,458 --> 00:19:42,666
Umbrasylvis shall be
on total lockdown

461
00:19:42,666 --> 00:19:44,750
until we determine who it was!

462
00:19:44,750 --> 00:19:46,791
The brigand must pay!

463
00:19:46,791 --> 00:19:48,291
You don't understand.

464
00:19:48,291 --> 00:19:49,916
We need to get back to--

465
00:19:49,916 --> 00:19:51,208
No one leaves here

466
00:19:51,208 --> 00:19:52,750
until someone is punished--

467
00:19:52,750 --> 00:19:55,291
So proclaims
the Grand Inquisitor!

468
00:19:55,291 --> 00:19:58,375
[crowd of citizens cheering]

469
00:19:58,375 --> 00:20:00,416
[♪♪♪]

470
00:20:00,416 --> 00:20:03,291
[knocking on gate]

471
00:20:05,458 --> 00:20:06,875
Senator Tartigrade!

472
00:20:06,875 --> 00:20:09,250
Always nice to see you,

473
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:12,500
but this is a strange hour
for a visit.

474
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:15,250
These are strange times,
Mr. Frohicky.

475
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:16,791
I need to talk to the Ninja.

476
00:20:16,791 --> 00:20:18,500
My apologies,

477
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:21,250
they are currently
in parts unknown.

478
00:20:21,250 --> 00:20:23,000
Cole's the only one in town,

479
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,166
but he's out

480
00:20:24,166 --> 00:20:26,875
investigating reports
of an energy monster.

481
00:20:26,875 --> 00:20:28,416
An energy monster?

482
00:20:28,416 --> 00:20:29,583
Where?

483
00:20:29,583 --> 00:20:31,000
The Crossroads.

484
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,041
Wow.

485
00:20:32,041 --> 00:20:34,125
That's exactly why I'm here.

486
00:20:34,125 --> 00:20:37,083
Imperium was invaded
by a strange energy creature.

487
00:20:37,083 --> 00:20:40,208
It caused a lot of damage,
then disappeared.

488
00:20:40,208 --> 00:20:41,583
I was hoping the Ninja

489
00:20:41,583 --> 00:20:43,625
could help us figure out
what it was.

490
00:20:43,625 --> 00:20:46,125
I'll tell Cole
as soon as he returns.

491
00:20:46,125 --> 00:20:47,000
Thank you,

492
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,291
we need the help.

493
00:20:48,291 --> 00:20:49,708
Imperium's infrastructure

494
00:20:49,708 --> 00:20:51,625
can't handle
more attacks like that.

495
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,458
[knocking in code]

496
00:21:15,375 --> 00:21:17,416
Bigger than I thought.

497
00:21:17,416 --> 00:21:18,916
I should've brought back-up.

498
00:21:18,916 --> 00:21:20,000
[Dr. LaRow]
Yes, you should have...

499
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:22,875
...but you didn't.

500
00:21:22,875 --> 00:21:23,875
Stun him,

501
00:21:23,875 --> 00:21:25,208
but keep him alive.

502
00:21:31,416 --> 00:21:32,541
[stun beam crackling]

503
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:37,666
A Ninja on our trail.

504
00:21:37,666 --> 00:21:39,208
How predictable.

505
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

